python -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\activate
4. Install packages
pip install openpyxl pyinstaller
5. Build the workbook logic in processor.py

Put all your Excel rules here.

Functions I’d suggest:

process_workbook(path_in, path_out)
fix_orientation_columns(ws)
build_feature_type_final(ws)
set_delta_columns(ws)

That keeps the code organized.

6. Build a simple GUI in main.py

Use tkinter:

one button to choose a file
one button to process it
success/error message box
7. Test it as a normal Python app first

Run:

python main.py

Do not package it yet. First make sure it processes a workbook correctly.

8. Package it into an .exe

PyInstaller’s basic command is pyinstaller myscript.py, and for a GUI app you generally want the windowed mode so no console opens.

Use:pyinstaller --onefile --noconsole --name ExcelCleaner main.py

Hey

That will create:

build\
dist\
a .spec file
PyInstaller documents that it writes a spec file and build folder during packaging.

Your executable will be in:

dist\main.exe